      "body": "Summary:\n\nRL has two distinct clocks. The optimizer step identifies the model version:\nstep 0 before training, then steps 1 through 150 in the reference run.\nW&B's internal _step identifies a committed logging entry. Once an entry is\ncommitted, W&B expects subsequent entries to advance its internal step.\n\nPreviously, WandBLogger passed the optimizer step to wandb.log as W&B's\ninternal step and committed every call. The observed sequence was:\n\n  Event                  Model version  Old W&B call             Outcome\n  Initial validation                 0  step=0, commit=True     Saved: 0.10\n  Final training metrics           150  step=150, commit=True   Saved; next step is 151\n  Final validation                 150  step=150, commit=True   Rejected as out of order\n\nThe final validation really ran: the 150-step DAPO run recorded 5/30 (0.17)\nheld-out correct answers in the console and rollout records, versus 3/30\n(0.10) before training. W&B's latest validation value stayed at 0.10\nbecause the initial validation was its only accepted validation entry.\nThe dashboard was therefore missing a result, not reporting that final\nvalidation failed or that the model still scored 0.10.\n\nSeparate model version from W&B event order. Add an optional step_metric to\nthe shared WandBLogger; when supplied, it registers that metric with\nwandb.define_metric as the axis for other metrics. RL opts in with\ntrainer/step. Every RL log payload includes trainer/step=<optimizer step>,\nbut wandb.log no longer receives that value as its internal step.\nCommitting a log entry can advance W&B's internal _step without advancing\nthe optimizer step.\n\nThe corrected sequence for the same run would be:\n\n  W&B entry 0:    trainer/step=0,   validation=0.10\n  W&B entry 150:  trainer/step=150, training metrics\n  W&B entry 151:  trainer/step=150, validation=0.17\n\nThe last two entries are consecutive W&B events for the same model\nversion. Both plot at trainer/step=150, so the final validation is kept in\nW&B history and its 0.17 becomes the latest validation summary value.\nCharts explicitly configured to use W&B's _step should instead use\ntrainer/step when they need optimizer steps on the x-axis.\n\nOnly the RL metrics processor enables this behavior. Console and\nTensorBoard retain the actual optimizer step, and other WandBLogger\ncallers keep explicit-step logging. Existing runs are not backfilled:\nthe fix prevents this loss of data on future runs.\n\nTest Plan:\n- 88 targeted CPU tests passed for RL metrics and WandBLogger.\n- Offline W&B smoke check: validation 0.10 at model step 0, training at\n  step 150, and validation 0.17 at model step 150; the W&B summary reports\n  0.17 at trainer/step=150.",
